# Agent guidance, guardrails and team process. Changes here change how every agent behaves, so
# they are reviewed by a collaborator other than the author.
#
# Every collaborator is listed deliberately. GitHub never requests review from the author of a
# pull request, and an author's own approval never satisfies a code-owner requirement, so listing
# everyone expresses "any collaborator except the author" without naming a single bottleneck.
# CODEOWNERS has no way to say that directly.
#
# This repository is under a personal account, so GitHub teams are unavailable and collaborators
# must be listed individually. Keep the list in step with:
#   gh api repos/keithfernandes12/young-illustrators-primer/collaborators --jq '.[].login'
#
# These lines route review requests; they do not gate the merge. `protect-main` sets
# require_code_owner_review=false, and the gate is required_approving_review_count=1 plus
# require_last_push_approval=true, which already prevents self-approval. Setting
# require_code_owner_review=true would change nothing while every collaborator is an owner.
#
# Decision of 2026-10-25 in docs/plans/ai-coding-framework.md (open question 1).

